Load an S3 object's properties from servers that keep no object ACLs.

DoLoadFileProperties reads the object's ACL before its tags and fails on any
error, so on a server that implements no object ACLs -- versitygw answers
GetObjectAcl with 501 NotImplemented, as do other S3-compatible servers --
the Properties dialog does not open at all, the tags included. A
NotImplemented answer now reads as an ACL with no grants; any other error
still fails as before. Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/S3FileSystem.cpp
+++ b/source/core/S3FileSystem.cpp
@@ -1869,1 +1869,1 @@
-    CheckLibS3Error(AclData);
+    if (AclData.Status == S3StatusErrorNotImplemented) { Properties.AclGrantCount = 0; } else { CheckLibS3Error(AclData); }
